  "title": "2026-07-29-eval-202743 · eval-harness-orchestration",
  "description": "# Offline evaluation harness orchestration\n\nShows a pinned, fingerprinted evaluation run moving left-to-right through immutable scenario inputs, bounded execution against an isolated system under test, evidence-backed grading, scorecard assembly, compatible baseline comparison, and retention/promotion.\n\n- **Execution:** the scheduler fans scenarios to a bounded worker pool. Workers run ordered steps, capture the full transcript and final artifact, retry infrastructure faults, and separately record product regressions.\n- **Grading:** globally bounded graders score criteria concurrently; the artifact-only grader is blind to the original request. Evidence is mandatory, with invalid verdicts retried and repeated failures flagged.\n- **Comparison:** valid verdicts become a scorecard. Threshold movements are narrated only when the chosen baseline has the same run fingerprint.\n- **Retention:** artifacts, transcripts, and verdicts remain available for review; a promoted compatible run becomes a future baseline.",
  "mode": "diagram",
